  "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $y=0$ and $z=0$ in the equation of the paraboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-5)^{2}-3(0-1)^{2} & =0+5 \\\\ 2(x-5)^{2}-3 & =5 \\\\ 2(x-5)^{2} & =8 \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =5\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solutions $x=3$ and $x=7.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(3,0,0)$ and $(7,0,0).$",
